      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you mind adding more context on this?\nYou could take it from the issue:\n\n```\nThe problem was introduced by Change 412064, which was released from v3.10 onwards.\n\nThat change avoids recomputing submit requirements by reusing post-review in-memory change data. However, the in-memory ChangeData can become stale if a review listener/plugin mutates the change during review event processing, for example by submitting the change or adding additional labels.\n\nIn that case, PostReview returns the ChangeInfo computed from the review update state, not from the final change state after listener-triggered mutation. The returned ChangeInfo is stale by definition and will be used by the UI to display an incorrect status.\n```",
